            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 18 manifest paths. The new --base flag value is validated by review.CheckRev in engine/review/app/chain.go before git reads it, and the test in engine/cmd/review_check_test.go covers a base beginning with '-' being refused, so no option injection reaches git.",
              "The chain walk in engine/review/app/chain.go keeps a visited-commit set, so it always terminates. Each commit is held by the same cleared function that backs the single-head check, which re-reads stored files and recomputes from git, so there is no weaker path to clearance.",
              "Without --base the code path calls Service.Check and prints the same output shape as before, so there is no regression for existing invocations. The cleared refactor in engine/review/app/check.go only renames variables.",
              "The chain follows only the first result's base as the next commit. This is documented, and every other result of the commit must still be clear, so no bypass is reachable.",
              "No secrets, dependency changes, or unsafe input handling were introduced."
            ]
          }
        }
