            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The CheckChain walk in engine/review/app/chain.go always terminates, because each step marks a commit as passed and a repeat is refused with ErrChainLoops.",
              "Any commit that is not cleared by a stored result or exemption, whether through a gap, a blocked or unclear result, or a differing binding, returns an error. The chain therefore never clears silently.",
              "The invocation without --base takes the original Check path, and the existing output is preserved by the shared cleared helper and checkedJSON. The new chain test exercises this case.",
              "The chain tests in engine/cmd/review_check_chain_test.go cover a clear chain, a chain ending in an exemption, a gap, an unclear range, a range that begins before the base, a loop, and the unchanged no-base output. The CLI tests cover a duplicate --base and a base that looks like an option.",
              "I did not see an unproved behavior that this change caused."
            ]
          }
        }
